&lt;div class=&quot;intent_sub_item Abstract__block&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;intent_sub_title Abstract__block__title mb-1 mt-3&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Purpose&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;intent_sub_content Abstract__block__text&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This study aims to offer a model solution for the educational ecosystem transformation to enable entrepreneurial responses to contemporary environmental challenges.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;intent_sub_item Abstract__block&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;intent_sub_title Abstract__block__title mb-1 mt-3&quot;&gt;Design/methodology/approach&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;intent_sub_content Abstract__block__text&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The research applies the grounded theory, the process-based approach, comparative analysis, data analysis, systematised literature review and the Quadruple Helix Model.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;intent_sub_item Abstract__block&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;intent_sub_title Abstract__block__title mb-1 mt-3&quot;&gt;Findings&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;intent_sub_content Abstract__block__text&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The “progressive” character and content in the Model are defined by the pedagogical approaches and purposes of entrepreneurial education instead of its association with a formal level of education, as it has been done so far. Among the findings are re-defined social entrepreneurship, specified teaching topics and pedagogical approaches supportive of social entrepreneurship competencies development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;intent_sub_item Abstract__block&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;intent_sub_title Abstract__block__title mb-1 mt-3&quot;&gt;Research limitations/implications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;intent_sub_content Abstract__block__text&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the light of further data and information, the future improvement of the model could well bring about the extension of some of its composite elements in the educational “input” and “output” dimensions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;intent_sub_item Abstract__block&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;intent_sub_title Abstract__block__title mb-1 mt-3&quot;&gt;Practical implications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;intent_sub_content Abstract__block__text&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An advantage of the proposed model can be drawn from its applicability as guidelines for the composition of social entrepreneurship content within academic courses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;intent_sub_item Abstract__block&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;intent_sub_title Abstract__block__title mb-1 mt-3&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Originality/value&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;intent_sub_content Abstract__block__text&quot;&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;The value of research findings is associated with the fact that social entrepreneurship remains an underdeveloped subject area, while we observe the urgent need, reinforced by the sustainability crisis, to build systemic change around social entrepreneurship to facilitate sustainable development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
